> 🚀 **Welcome to the Machine Learning module of the Saylani Mass IT Training (SMIT) Data Science & Artificial Intelligence program!**

This directory contains **Jupyter notebooks, practical assignments, data-processing workflows, and hands-on projects** covering machine learning algorithms, model evaluation, feature engineering, and deployment.

---

## 🧠 What You'll Learn

```text
📊 Data
   │
   ▼
🧹 Preprocessing
   │
   ▼
🔎 Exploratory Data Analysis
   │
   ▼
⚙️ Feature Engineering
   │
   ▼
🤖 Model Training
   │
   ▼
📈 Evaluation & Optimization
   │
   ▼
💾 Model Persistence
   │
   ▼
🚀 Deployment
```

---

## 📂 Module Topics & Structure

| #      | Topic                        | What You'll Learn                                                          | Tools                        |
| ------ | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| **01** | 📊 **EDA & Preprocessing**   | Data cleaning, scaling, encoding, missing values & outlier detection       | `Pandas` `NumPy` `Seaborn`   |
| **02** | 📈 **Regression**            | Linear, Polynomial, Ridge & Lasso Regression                               | `Scikit-Learn` `Statsmodels` |
| **03** | 🎯 **Classification**        | Logistic Regression, Decision Trees, Random Forest, SVM, KNN & Naive Bayes | `Scikit-Learn`               |
| **04** | 📏 **Model Evaluation**      | Confusion Matrix, Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC & Cross-Validation        | `Scikit-Learn`               |
| **05** | 🚀 **Ensemble & Boosting**   | Bagging, AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost & Stacking                   | `XGBoost` `Scikit-Learn`     |
| **06** | 🔮 **Unsupervised Learning** | K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering, DBSCAN, PCA & t-SNE                      | `Scikit-Learn` `Matplotlib`  |
| **07** | 🌐 **Model Deployment**      | Saving models and creating APIs / applications                             | `Joblib` `Streamlit` `Flask` |

---

## 📊 01. Exploratory Data Analysis & Preprocessing

Learn how to transform raw data into clean, machine-learning-ready data.

### 🔧 Topics

* 🧹 Data Cleaning
* 🔍 Exploratory Data Analysis
* 🕳️ Handling Missing Values
* 📦 Outlier Detection
* ⚖️ Standardization
* 📏 Normalization
* 🔤 Categorical Encoding
* 🛠️ Feature Engineering

**Libraries:** `Pandas` `NumPy` `Seaborn`

---

## 📈 02. Supervised Learning – Regression

Learn how machines predict **continuous numerical values**.

### Algorithms

* Linear Regression
* Polynomial Regression
* Ridge Regression
* Lasso Regression

### 📏 Evaluation Metrics

* MAE
* MSE
* RMSE
* R² Score

**Libraries:** `Scikit-Learn` `Statsmodels`

---

## 🎯 03. Supervised Learning – Classification

Learn how machine learning models classify data into different categories.

### 🤖 Algorithms

```text
Logistic Regression
       ↓
Decision Trees
       ↓
Random Forest
       ↓
SVM
       ↓
KNN
       ↓
Naive Bayes
```

**Library:** `Scikit-Learn`

---

## 📏 04. Model Evaluation & Optimization

A model isn't useful just because it makes predictions — we need to know **how well it performs**.

### 📊 Evaluation

* Confusion Matrix
* Accuracy
* Precision
* Recall
* F1-Score
* ROC-AUC

### 🔄 Optimization

* Cross-Validation
* GridSearchCV
* RandomizedSearchCV
* Hyperparameter Tuning

---

## 🚀 05. Ensemble Methods & Boosting

Combine multiple models to create stronger and more accurate machine-learning systems.

### 🌳 Techniques

* Bagging
* AdaBoost
* Gradient Boosting
* XGBoost
* Stacking Classifiers

**Libraries:** `Scikit-Learn` `XGBoost`

---

## 🔮 06. Unsupervised Learning

Discover hidden patterns in data **without predefined labels**.

### 🧩 Clustering

* K-Means
* Hierarchical Clustering
* DBSCAN

### 📉 Dimensionality Reduction

* PCA
* t-SNE

**Libraries:** `Scikit-Learn` `Matplotlib`

---

## 🌐 07. Model Persistence & Deployment

Take trained machine-learning models from notebooks into real applications.

### 💾 Model Persistence

```python
import joblib

joblib.dump(model, "model.pkl")

model = joblib.load("model.pkl")
```

### 🚀 Deployment Tools

* Flask
* Streamlit
* REST APIs
* Model Serialization

---

